    "description": "Critical safety guardrails for protected branches: never commit, push, or force-push directly to main, latest, or release branches; no destructive history rewrites without explicit user approval. Use before any git operation that touches protected branches, before force-push, reset --hard, history rewrite, or branch deletion, or whenever the user asks about merging, pushing, or release branches.",
